# VI on the mixed omega with a MEAN-FIELD q -- the diagonal-covariance arm.
#
# The claim under test, from docs/estimation/vi.qmd (line ~151): mean_field costs "a looser
# bound whenever the true posterior is correlated, which for CL/V it almost always is". That
# rests on theory alone today, and section 4.9 makes `emvi` the external check because the two
# families match by name (`viFamily = "meanField"`).
#
# Everything but `vi_family` is identical to vi_block_closed_form.ferx, deliberately -- the
# correlated (ETA_CL, ETA_V) block is the whole point, since on a diagonal Omega the two
# families have nothing to disagree about (family_tests.rs:499 pins them as exactly equal
# there).
#
# WHAT THIS ARM CAN AND CANNOT SHOW. Measured 2026-08-20, this arm converges to a sigma 14.5%
# below the full_rank arm's (0.011863 vs 0.013878), which moves its Laplace OFV by 8 units.
# The two -2*ELBO values therefore sit at DIFFERENT (theta, Omega, sigma), and the ELBO is a
# bound on -2 log L at whatever parameter vector it was evaluated. So the difference between
# the arms is a mixture of the family effect and the parameter difference, and it does NOT
# isolate bound looseness. Reported here as a directional observation only.
#
# Isolating the family effect needs both q families evaluated at ONE parameter vector, which
# no CLI option reaches today -- it is a Tier-1 unit test over elbo_agq_bound.rs, in the shape
# family_tests.rs already uses (it loops the families over a fixed fixture). That test, not
# this arm, is what would actually close the vi.qmd claim.
#
# elbo_tightness_ratio is NOT the measure to read for looseness either: it is excess over
# Sum(d_i/2), a health diagnostic (elbo.rs:1067) whose denominator is d=3 for both families.
[parameters]
  theta TVCL(0.13, 0.001, 10.0)
  theta TVV(8.0, 0.1, 500.0)
  theta TVKA(1.0, 0.01, 50.0)

  block_omega (ETA_CL, ETA_V) = [0.09, 0.02, 0.04]
  omega ETA_KA ~ 0.30

  sigma PROP_ERR ~ 0.1 (sd)

[individual_parameters]
  CL = TVCL * exp(ETA_CL)
  V  = TVV  * exp(ETA_V)
  KA = TVKA * exp(ETA_KA)

[structural_model]
  pk one_cpt_oral(cl=CL, v=V, ka=KA)

[error_model]
  DV ~ proportional(PROP_ERR)

[fit_options]
  method = vi
  vi_family = mean_field
  # 128 draws, not the default 8. The convergence rule stops when the ELBO's drift falls below
  # its own Monte-Carlo noise floor, and at 8 draws it does so while real drift remains: on this
  # model that left the fit 9.4 OFV short of AGQ. More draws, not more iterations, is the lever
  # (docs/estimation/vi.qmd, "How sigma is updated"). A comparison run must be converged or it
  # measures the stopping rule rather than the estimator.
  vi_mc_samples = 128
  vi_omega_update = closed_form
  vi_final_ofv = laplace
